{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Lateralus and Aenima feel like natural next choices after 10.000 Days because I want more of Tool's intricate rhythms and progressive heaviness.",
    "Toxicity fits because its unusual rhythms and memorable heavy songs connect with what appeals to me in Tool and Disturbed."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Be Not Nobody's piano-led pop and No Pads, No Helmets...Just Balls' lighter pop-punk do not match the heavier, more intricate music I want today.",
    "Vile offers intensity, but its relentless death-metal approach misses the melody and rhythmic complexity that make heavy music appealing to me right now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Heavy guitars and aggression alone seem to count too much; I can find an album relevant without wanting to choose it over Tool today.",
    "My earlier interest in pop-punk and accessible rock seems to carry too much weight compared with my latest interest in Tool and Disturbed."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My latest interaction with 10.000 Days makes exploring more Tool especially appealing right now.",
    "I am looking for heaviness with intricate rhythms and memorable songs, so greater intensity does not automatically mean a better match."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in heavy music, but only some capture my current preference for intricate rhythms and melodic heaviness."
}"}
